1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 f5 4. d3 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. O-O Be7 7. a3 O-O 8. Bc4+ Kh8 9. Ng5 Qe8 10. Ne6 Bxe6 11. Bxe6 fxe4 12. dxe4 Nd4 13. Ba2 $6 (13. Bc4 $1) 13... Qg6 14. f3 Nh5 15. Kh1 $2 (15. f4 $1) 15... Bg5 16. Bxg5 Qxg5 17. Ne2 Rf6 ({This allows subsequent counter-play in the centre. The immediate} 17... Nxe2 {followed by ...Nf4 gives Black the advantage.}) 18. Nxd4 exd4 19. Qxd4 Rh6 20. Rfe1 Rf8 21. Rad1 {with back rank mating threats after his next move.} Qh4 22. e5 $1 Ng3+ 23. Kg1 Qxh2+ 24. Kf2 dxe5 (24... Nf5 $1) 25. Rxe5 $2 (25. Qb4 $1 Rhf6 26. Qa4 {would prolong the game into an ending.}) 25... Rg6 26. Rd2 Ne4+ $1 27. Qxe4 ({The game finish given as} 27. Rxe4 Rxg2+ 28. Ke3 Rxf3+ 29. Kxf3 Qg3# {on 2022 Mega Database.}) 27... Rxg2+ 28. Ke3 Rxf3+ $1 {Sources: John Littlewood; CHESS, 21 October 1960, Vol.26/373, p46} 0-1

