{Donner now played} 1. Bxg7 (1. Bb4 $1 $18) 1... Kxg7 2. Rc1 {with a strong game - pawn up, weak pawns at a6, e4; pin on the c-file. Penrose soon had to give up the exchange but found (or was given) unexpected chances and Donner finally conceded the draw. Yet in the diagram Donner had a move which Penrose intended to answer by resigning! Source: CHESS, 21 October 1960, Vol.26/373, p50} 1/2-1/2

